---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'June 9, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - ScoreSpace"
  description="How ScoreSpace, Inc. collects, uses, and protects your information across our website and published games."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ScoreSpace, Inc.</strong> ("ScoreSpace,"
        "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, discloses, and protects information about you when
        you visit <a href="https://scorespace.net">scorespace.net</a> (the "Site"), participate
        in our game jams, join our community, or play games we publish on third-party platforms
        such as Discord, Reddit, and others (collectively, the "Services").
      </p>
      <p>
        By using the Services, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance
        with this Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the Services.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        ScoreSpace, Inc. is a community-powered game publisher. We host monthly game jams,
        operate a community, and publish games that run on third-party platforms. For privacy
        questions, contact us at <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect the following categories of information:</p>

      <h3>2.1 Information you provide to us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Contact details (such as your email address) when you reach out to us, sign up for
          updates, or submit an entry to a game jam.
        </li>
        <li>
          Content you submit, such as game jam submissions, comments, ratings, and feedback.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.2 Information from games we publish on third-party platforms</h3>
      <p>
        When you play a game we publish on a platform such as Discord or Reddit, we may receive
        information made available to us by that platform, which can include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your platform account identifier and username or display name (for example, your
          Discord user ID or Reddit username).
        </li>
        <li>
          Gameplay data such as scores, progress, in-game actions, session activity, and
          interactions with other players.
        </li>
        <li>
          Technical information such as approximate locale/language, device or client type, and
          timestamps, where provided by the platform.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We generally do <strong>not</strong> receive your password, payment card numbers, or
        private messages from these platforms. The information we receive depends on the
        platform and the permissions you grant.
      </p>

      <h3>2.3 Information collected automatically on the Site</h3>
      <p>
        The Site is a static website. We aim to keep automatic data collection to a minimum.
        Standard server logs and content-delivery providers may process limited technical data
        (such as IP address, browser type, and pages requested) to deliver and secure the Site.
        The Site loads web fonts from Google Fonts, which may receive your IP address as part of
        serving those fonts.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate, maintain, and improve the Services and our games;</li>
        <li>Run game jams, track submissions, and recognize participants and winners;</li>
        <li>Display leaderboards, scores, and other gameplay features;</li>
        <li>Communicate with you, respond to inquiries, and send updates you request;</li>
        <li>Monitor for fraud, abuse, cheating, and violations of our Terms;</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations and enforce our agreements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we share information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>With third-party platforms:</strong> Games we publish run on platforms such as
          Discord and Reddit. Your use of those games is also governed by the platform's own
          terms and privacy policies, and certain information (such as your username, scores, or
          public activity) may be visible to other users on that platform.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>With service providers:</strong> Vendors who host, analyze, or support the
          Services on our behalf, under obligations of confidentiality.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>For legal reasons:</strong> When required by law, or to protect the rights,
          safety, and property of ScoreSpace, our users, or the public.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>In a business transfer:</strong> In connection with a merger, acquisition,
          financing, or sale of assets.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Third-party platforms and services</h2>
      <p>
        The Services rely on and link to third-party platforms, including Discord, Reddit,
        itch.io, and others. These platforms are operated by independent companies and have their
        own privacy practices. We encourage you to review their policies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://discord.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.reddit.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reddit Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://itch.io/docs/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">itch.io Privacy Policy</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>We are not responsible for the privacy practices of these third parties.</p>

      <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information for as long as necessary to provide the Services, comply with our
        legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. Gameplay and jam records
        may be retained to maintain leaderboards, historical archives, and statistics.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict
        the use of your personal information, or to object to certain processing. Residents of the
        EEA/UK (under the GDPR) and California (under the CCPA/CPRA) may have additional rights,
        including the right not to be discriminated against for exercising them. To make a
        request, contact us at <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>. We
        may need to verify your identity before responding.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children under 13. Some platforms we publish on (such as
        Discord) require users to be at least 13, and higher in some jurisdictions. If you believe
        a child has provided us with personal information, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a> and we will take
        appropriate steps to delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>9. International users</h2>
      <p>
        ScoreSpace is based in the United States, and the Services are operated there. If you
        access the Services from outside the United States, your information may be transferred to,
        stored, and processed in the United States and other countries with different data
        protection laws than your own.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable measures to protect your information. However, no method of
        transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the
        "Last updated" date above. Your continued use of the Services after changes take effect
        constitutes acceptance of the revised Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:legal@scorespace.net">legal@scorespace.net</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-footer-note">
        See also our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}terms/`}>Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-bg-secondary) 0%, var(--color-bg) 100%);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: white;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .legal h3 {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal li {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
